course: dictionary
lesson: 10328
title: Tragic, the many meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «The news of the flood was tragic: many families lost their homes.» Here tragic means very sad, because people suffered something terrible.
explain: In English lessons, tragic means to do with a tragedy, a serious play or story that ends in disaster for the main character. A tragic hero is the main character whose story ends badly. Look for clues like play, hero or ending.
explain: In playground talk, «tragic» is slang for really bad, as in «His dancing is tragic.» Nobody is hurt; it is a joke about how embarrassing something is. Ask yourself: is someone hurt or dead? Then it means very sad. Is it a play? Then it means tragedy. Is it a joke about being bad? Then it is slang.
fact: Tragic means very sad, usually because someone has died or suffered something terrible.
fact: A tragedy is a serious play or story that ends in disaster for the main character.
fact: «Tragic» is slang for really bad, as in «His dancing is tragic.»
fact: Phrases: a tragic accident, tragic news, a tragic hero, a tragic ending.
fact: Tragic, more tragic, most tragic: it is an adjective, so it describes a noun.
exercise: «The flood left many families with nothing. The news was tragic.» What does tragic mean here? | *Very sad, because people suffered something terrible | A play with a happy ending | Really bad at dancing | Funny and silly
exercise: Ms Patel says, «The hero of our play has a tragic ending.» What does tragic mean here? | Lost in the woods | Embarrassingly bad | Very loud | *A story that ends in disaster for the main character
exercise: Aisha laughs and says, «Your singing is tragic!» What does tragic mean here? | *Embarrassingly bad, as slang | A serious play | Very sad because someone died
test: In «The tragic hero died at the end of the play.» what kind of story is this? | A comedy | A cartoon | *A tragedy | A news report
test: Which sentence uses tragic as slang? | «The tragic flood took many homes.» | «The tragic accident closed the road.» | «The tragic news made the whole town cry.» | *«His dancing is tragic, honestly.»
exam: Ben asks, «Does tragic always mean very sad?» What is the best answer? | Yes, always, in every sentence | No, it is a colour | Yes, but only in maths | *No, in playground talk it can mean embarrassingly bad
